body:
@clintongormley 
It is matching `POST /{index}/{type}` handler.
It is trying to create dynamic mapping for type `_settings`, but can't and throws MapperParsingException.

I cannot reproduce this issue in `7.0` ( 95dea2408d4c6b70fe43ea3d4294dd98f89178b1 )
I think the current behavior ( shown below ) is correct and this issue can be closed.

```
curl -XPUT "http://localhost:9200/index1/_settings?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json'
```
```
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "parse_exception",
        "reason" : "request body is required"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "parse_exception",
    "reason" : "request body is required"
  },
  "status" : 400
}
```

```
curl -XPUT "http://localhost:9200/index1/_settings?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'
```
```
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "action_request_validation_exception",
        "reason" : "Validation Failed: 1: no settings to update;"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "action_request_validation_exception",
    "reason" : "Validation Failed: 1: no settings to update;"
  },
  "status" : 400
}
```
Also using unsupported op `POST` is correctly detected and reported
```
curl -XPOST "http://localhost:9200/index1/_settings?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'
```
```
{
  "error" : "Incorrect HTTP method for uri [/index1/_settings?pretty] and method [POST], allowed: [PUT, GET]",
  "status" : 405
}
```
